# *** PROTECTED PRODUCER BYTES. Do not remove or narrow. ***
# tools/ci_candidate_evidence.py::_protected_producer_manifest hashes the RAW
# WORKING-TREE BYTES of each file below and refuses any that differs from its
# committed blob. Without an explicit eol pin, a Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true materialises CRLF while the blob holds LF, and the producer
# then refuses its own files -- the evidence gate cannot run at all.
#
# This is not hypothetical: it has cost hosted runs on this campaign, and
# `git hash-object` will NOT reveal it, because that command applies the same
# autocrlf filter and reports a false match. Compare raw bytes, not filtered
# hashes.
#
# .gitattributes itself is pinned AND bound into the producer manifest, so this
# guarantee cannot be silently withdrawn by editing this file.
.gitattributes text eol=lf
